      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Hardened Evidence Collector Shell Script with Error Isolation &amp; Jittered Retries
      </h2>
      <p>
        When executing automated CLI calls against cloud provider APIs, intermittent network timeouts or API throttling (e.g. AWS <code>ThrottlingException</code> or GitHub <code>403 Rate Limit Exceeded</code>) can silently fail evidence generation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The shell script below implements defensive bash flags (<code>set -euo pipefail</code>), randomized exponential backoff (full jitter), and isolated error trapping to ensure that a failure in one criteria extraction does not corrupt the entire evidence bundle:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-emerald-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Hardened Evidence Collector Engine with Error Isolation
set -euo pipefail

OUTPUT_DIR="evidence-bundle"
mkdir -p "$OUTPUT_DIR"

log() {
  echo "[$(date -u +'%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')] [INFO] $1"
}

log_warn() {
  echo "[$(date -u +'%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')] [WARN] $1" >&2
}

# Exponential backoff retry helper with randomized jitter
retry_command() {
  local max_attempts=5
  local delay=2
  local attempt=1
  local cmd="$@"

  until $cmd; do
    if [ $attempt -ge $max_attempts ]; then
      log_warn "Command '$cmd' failed after $attempt attempts."
      return 1
    fi
    # Add random jitter between 0 and 2 seconds
    local jitter=$(( RANDOM % 3 ))
    local total_delay=$(( delay + jitter ))
    log_warn "Attempt $attempt failed! Retrying in ${total_delay}s..."
    sleep $total_delay
    delay=$(( delay * 2 ))
    attempt=$(( attempt + 1 ))
  done
}

# 1. AWS KMS Key Rotation Verification (CC6.7)
log "Extracting KMS key rotation policies..."
retry_command aws kms list-keys --query 'Keys[*].KeyId' --output text | tr '\t' '\n' | while read -r key_id; do
  aws kms get-key-rotation-status --key-id "$key_id" >> "$OUTPUT_DIR/kms-rotation-status.json" 2>/dev/null || true
done

# 2. AWS GuardDuty Detector Findings (CC7.2)
log "Extracting active GuardDuty threat telemetry..."
DETECTOR_ID=$(aws guardduty list-detectors --query 'DetectorIds[0]' --output text)
if [ -n "$DETECTOR_ID" ] &amp;&amp; [ "$DETECTOR_ID" != "None" ]; then
  aws guardduty get-detector --detector-id "$DETECTOR_ID" > "$OUTPUT_DIR/guardduty-detector-config.json"
fi

# 3. Finalize Checksums
log "Generating manifest..."
(cd "$OUTPUT_DIR" &amp;&amp; sha256sum * > SHA256SUMS.txt)
log "Evidence extraction successfully completed."</code></pre>

