      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Top 4 Production CI/CD Compliance Failure Modes &amp; Real-Time Remediation Runbook
      </h2>
      <p>
        When operating automated continuous compliance pipelines, unexpected infrastructure drift can cause scheduled workflows to fail. Here is the operational runbook for diagnosing and remediating the top 4 failure modes:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-4 text-slate-300">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">1. IAM Credential Report Generation Race Condition:</strong> The command <code>aws iam generate-credential-report</code> is asynchronous. If the script immediately attempts to download the report before AWS finishes compiling it, the API throws a <code>ReportInProgressException</code>. <em>Remediation:</em> Implement a polling loop checking <code>aws iam get-credential-report --query 'State'</code> until state equals <code>COMPLETE</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">2. GitHub Actions OIDC Subject Token Mismatch:</strong> If your repository is renamed, transferred, or the workflow branch shifts from <code>main</code> to <code>master</code>, the OIDC subject claim (<code>sub</code>) will fail AWS STS policy validation, throwing an <code>AccessDeniedException: Not authorized to assume role</code>. <em>Remediation:</em> Update your IAM Role Trust Relationship <code>token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub</code> condition to match the exact repository path.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">3. S3 Object Lock Retention Date in the Past:</strong> If your CI script calculates the retention date using an improper timezone or string syntax, the S3 API returns <code>InvalidArgument: The retain-until date must be in the future</code>. <em>Remediation:</em> Always format dates via <code>date -u -d "+365 days" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ</code> ensuring strict UTC formatting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">4. GitHub Personal Access Token Expiration for Branch Protections:</strong> When fetching branch protection rules via <code>gh api</code>, expired fine-grained PATs cause silent HTTP 401/403 authorization failures. <em>Remediation:</em> Utilize a GitHub App installation token or periodically rotate audit bot secrets with automated Slack expiry warnings.
        </li>
      </ul>

